Q: Visual Studio Community 2019 creates a project but cannot open the project it created? A: <p>I think you have missed the OutputType in Project file, So that, it's not working properly. Please add the property  <code>&lt;OutputType&gt;Exe&lt;/OutputType&gt;</code>.
Let me know, whether it's worked for you or not</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;Project Sdk=&quot;Microsoft.NET.Sdk&quot;&gt;

&lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
    &lt;OutputType&gt;Exe&lt;/OutputType&gt;
  &lt;TargetFramework&gt;netcoreapp3.0&lt;/TargetFramework&gt;
&lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;

&lt;/Project&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: java checkstyle rules debugging A: <ul>
<li>add property <code>maximum</code>.</li>
<li>add <code>s+</code> to accept any space or tab or others.</li>
</ul>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;module name=&quot;RegexpMultiline&quot;&gt;
    &lt;property name=&quot;id&quot; value=&quot;footerCopyright&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;property name=&quot;format&quot; value=&quot;(?s)/\*\s*Copyright\s+\(c\)\s+company\s+name\s+\d{4}\s+ALL\s+RIGHTS\s+RESERVED\s*\*/[\s\r\n]*\z&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;property name=&quot;message&quot; value=&quot;File must end with exact copyright footer. /* Copyright (c) company name 20xx ALL RIGHTS RESERVED */&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;property name=&quot;minimum&quot; value=&quot;1&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;property name=&quot;maximum&quot; value=&quot;1&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/module&gt;
</code></pre>
